 "notes": "ALPS light-shining-through-a-wall (LSW) at DESY (5 T HERA dipole, l=4.3 m each side). Headline pseudoscalar ALP-photon limit g_- from Fig. 4 left (e-print pics/alpminus.pdf), extracted from the vector fill paths as the lower (least-coupling) boundary of the ALPS excluded region, combining the vacuum run (red) and the Ar-gas run (orange) that fills the vacuum resonance gaps at higher mass. Paper Eq.(1) L=-(g_-/4)F Ftilde phi matches the canonical AxionPhoton convention, so g_- = g_agamma directly (no conversion). Axes calibrated from tick strokes; low-mass flat value ~6.5e-8 GeV^-1 cross-checked against Table 1 P_95%=2.25e-25 via P=(gBl/2)^4 giving 6.5e-8 GeV^-1. High-mass oscillatory structure reflects sin^2(M^2 l/4w) resonances. 95% C.L. LSW laboratory limit; no DM density assumed. The scalar counterpart g_+ (Fig.4 right) and hidden-photon (Fig.5)/MCP (Fig.6) limits are also given but AxionPhoton pseudoscalar is the main ALP result.",
